WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.755
A module shows text in menus, forms, messages and notifications, and translators need

00:00:06.755 --> 00:00:09.348
to find every one of those strings.

00:00:09.348 --> 00:00:16.620
In this video, we'll declare strings with localizers, handle plurals, and extract a template for translators.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:26.266
In Orchard Core, the English text you write in code is the key of its translation.

00:00:26.266 --> 00:00:30.279
A translation is found by that text and its context, the type or

00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:31.885
view that asks for it.

00:00:31.885 --> 00:00:35.210
Without a translation, the text is shown as written.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:38.458
A module registers nothing for this.

00:00:38.458 --> 00:00:41.968
It asks for a localizer through dependency injection.

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:47.500
Until the Localization feature is enabled, every localizer returns its text as written.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:56.758
In a service, a controller or a driver, inject an IStringLocalizer of your

00:00:56.758 --> 00:00:59.792
own type, usually kept in a field named S.

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:04.660
Index it with the English text, and pass any format arguments after it.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:11.566
An IHtmlLocalizer, usually named H, is for messages that carry HTML, and it

00:01:11.566 --> 00:01:14.226
encodes its format arguments.

00:01:14.226 --> 00:01:21.370
In Razor views, T is an IViewLocalizer, and in Liquid the t filter localizes through it.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:29.452
The context of a localizer is the full name of its type.

00:01:29.452 --> 00:01:35.714
Text from an IStringLocalizer of MyService has the context MyNamespace.MyService, which is the

00:01:35.714 --> 00:01:38.720
message context of its entry in a PO file.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:43.841
In a view, the context is the module ID, then Views, then the

00:01:43.841 --> 00:01:46.777
path of the view without its extension.

00:01:46.777 --> 00:01:52.910
The Welcome view in the Views folder of MyModule has the context MyModule.Views.Welcome.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:57.950
When no entry has the context, an entry without a context is used.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:04.147
To share one context between several types, create the localizer from the IStringLocalizerFactory,

00:02:04.147 --> 00:02:07.960
with a type, or with a context name and an empty location.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.468
The Plural extension takes a count, a singular form and a plural form.

00:02:16.468 --> 00:02:21.626
The count fills placeholder zero, and any arguments you add start at placeholder one.

00:02:21.626 --> 00:02:25.650
This call from the Features module lists the features it enabled.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.270
A translation lists one string for each form of its language.

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:34.428
The Plural-Forms header of the PO file, or else the plural rule of

00:02:34.428 --> 00:02:37.200
the culture, selects the form for a count.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:42.454
Do not hardcode the number in the text, because languages count differently.

00:02:42.454 --> 00:02:46.409
To show the count, put placeholder zero in both forms, so that the

00:02:46.409 --> 00:02:48.990
translation decides where the count goes.

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:52.971
Orchard Core uses Plural itself.

00:02:52.971 --> 00:02:57.832
On the Manage Content page, which the Content Items menu item opens, the

00:02:57.832 --> 00:03:03.753
summary above the rows counts the items, and with several items it shows the plural form.

00:03:04.215 --> 00:03:08.585
Let's type About in the search box, and press Enter to filter the list.

00:03:09.043 --> 00:03:12.717
One item matches, so the summary shows the singular form.

00:03:12.717 --> 00:03:17.733
Both counts in the summary come from Plural, with the count in placeholder zero.

00:03:21.933 --> 00:03:26.748
Some text is declared where no localizer exists, such as the description of

00:03:26.748 --> 00:03:28.948
a permission in a static field.

00:03:28.948 --> 00:03:34.179
LocalizationSource keeps the English text together with the type that owns it, and

00:03:34.179 --> 00:03:36.913
translates, formats and encodes nothing.

00:03:37.663 --> 00:03:40.192
Translate it where it is displayed.

00:03:40.192 --> 00:03:47.162
The Localize extension of an IStringLocalizerFactory, or of an IHtmlLocalizerFactory, creates the localizer

00:03:47.162 --> 00:03:51.603
of the source's type and looks the text up in the current culture.

00:03:52.353 --> 00:03:58.997
Text that several modules share, such as Settings, is declared once in CommonLocalizationSources,

00:03:58.997 --> 00:04:00.997
so it is translated once.

00:04:00.997 --> 00:04:06.803
A module keeps its other sources in an internal static class named after the module.

00:04:11.003 --> 00:04:12.996
Translators see only the text.

00:04:12.996 --> 00:04:17.425
Explain it with the Note extension, name each format argument with the Arg

00:04:17.425 --> 00:04:22.076
helper, or put a comment starting with TRANSLATORS on the line above the call.

00:04:22.076 --> 00:04:24.733
None of these changes anything at runtime.

00:04:25.483 --> 00:04:32.111
Analyzers in the OrchardCore.Abstractions package check localizer calls as you type, and in every build.

00:04:32.111 --> 00:04:36.811
A key that is not a constant, or a LocalizationSource without a context,

00:04:36.811 --> 00:04:39.523
cannot be extracted, so it is reported.

00:04:43.723 --> 00:04:47.149
Translators work from a template, not from your code.

00:04:47.149 --> 00:04:53.130
Add the OrchardCore.Localization.Build package to each project whose strings should be extracted.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:57.833
Referencing it only from the application does not cover the other projects.

00:04:58.583 --> 00:05:02.824
A normal build only embeds the template that is already checked in.

00:05:02.824 --> 00:05:07.994
To write it, run the UpdateLocalizationCatalog target on one project, or build with

00:05:07.994 --> 00:05:13.803
UpdateLocalizationCatalogs set to true to update every project you build that has the package.

00:05:14.553 --> 00:05:19.622
The template is a POT file named after the assembly, next to the project file.

00:05:19.622 --> 00:05:24.692
Each entry has its context, its English text, your notes and format arguments,

00:05:24.692 --> 00:05:26.563
and an empty translation.

00:05:26.563 --> 00:05:28.373
Commit it with the code.

00:05:29.123 --> 00:05:36.154
Extraction reads C# localizer calls and LocalizationSource declarations, Razor views, and Liquid files

00:05:36.154 --> 00:05:39.083
where the t filter gets a literal text.

00:05:39.083 --> 00:05:43.835
A call it cannot resolve is reported with an OCLOC code, instead of

00:05:43.835 --> 00:05:45.853
becoming a guessed entry.

00:05:46.603 --> 00:05:51.249
A helper that only forwards the keys of its callers is not a declaration.

00:05:51.249 --> 00:05:57.953
Mark it with the SkipLocalizationExtraction attribute, and extraction ignores the localizer calls inside it.

00:05:58.703 --> 00:06:04.970
To gather the templates for a platform such as Crowdin, build with LocalizationCatalogOutputPath

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:06.445
set to one folder.

00:06:06.445 --> 00:06:10.992
Each template lands in a subfolder named after its target framework.

00:06:10.992 --> 00:06:17.013
Upload them as source files, and download the translated PO files into a supported location.

00:06:19.013 --> 00:06:24.718
Declare strings with localizers, plurals and sources, add notes where translators need them,

00:06:24.718 --> 00:06:27.047
and extract the template for them.

00:06:27.047 --> 00:06:30.889
A separate video covers installing and writing the PO files.

00:06:30.889 --> 00:06:32.403
Thanks for watching.

